    "justification": "The study is a preregistered, single-execution numerical screening of a design space: collisionless prescribed-field test-particle electron orbits (orbit_mc 1.7, numpy CPU) integrated in the accepted linear-vacuum L1a equivalent-current fields of every one of the 96 accepted geometry-sweep-v2 designs, re-solved on the CPU with identity proven against the sealed sweep record. Its recorded outcome is an accepted screening dataset (campaign status accepted_screening_dataset): per-design wall-hit, reflection, escape and timeout probabilities with Wilson intervals at two timesteps, a per-design convergence flag, per-cell and per-stratum counts, and a coupling-consumer record. The framework admits accepted numerical evidence through a typed committed manifest, hashed artifacts at a resolvable revision, exact registered claim text and generated artifacts with provenance sidecars; that pattern is applied here through the numerical-screening gate GATE-WALL-LOSS-GEOMETRY-SCREENING-V1 at the recorded outcome accepted-screening-dataset, a fourth outcome value added for this study. The fields are L1a screening fields and not P2-qualified, so nothing here is accepted physical-orbit evidence of the kind admitted by GATE-WALL-LOSS-V4; it is not the L1 field-resolved reduction of GATE-L1 (no manufactured solution, no refinement study beyond the four representatives' diagnostic, no L0 mapping, no performance model), not L2 and not L3, and it opens none of those gates. The dataset is surrogate and optimisation input only when carried with its label.",
